      "remediation": {
        "description": "Function URL Cors block combines AllowOrigins containing \"*\" with AllowCredentials set to true. Browsers refuse this combination, and the configuration signals unreasoned cross-origin policy.",
        "action": "Update the function URL config via \"aws lambda update-function-url-config --function-name \u003cname\u003e --cors '...'\" with either AllowCredentials set to false or an AllowOrigins list that enumerates specific origins. If the function handles sensitive operations, also confirm AuthType is AWS_IAM (see CTL.LAMBDA.URL.AUTH.001).",
